For that combination.... possibly.  For savefiles to be compatible,
you must be running games on both sites with the same configuration
settings (ie, identical, or nearly so, config.h).  You must be running
the same version.  You cannot switch platform (ie, x86 based systems
cannot swap files with PowerPC systems due to the big endian/little
endian incompatibility).  Finally, save games on the linux box will be
named <uid><name>.<comp> where uid is the uid of your user account,
name is the character name you're playing, and comp is the standard
extension of your compression utility (gz for gzip, Z for compress...
possibly zip for WinZip on windows).

Of course, there may be other reasons that say, outright, no!  I don't
know about them, and have never bothered...

